# Defect 382, 2026-10-06. An array literal was built by one copying
# `hero_array_push` per element, each handing back a new block: n+1 blocks for
# n elements and n(n+1)/2 element copies, paid again at every read of a
# `constant`, which is a function that builds its value. The C below builds
# each literal in the block `hero_array_new` sizes to it, one
# `hero_array_push_owned` per element copying it in where it lies: the
# constant of numbers, the constant of counted strings, and a literal in a
# function's body.
#
# 2026-10-06, panel 195: each constant below is now also laid out, a static
# block under `#if HERO_STATIC_CONSTANTS`, and the one-block build this case
# was written for stands under its `#else`, which a build under
# AddressSanitizer compiles; the literal in `main`'s body is built as before.

constant DIGITS: [i64]
    [3, 1, 4]

constant WORDS: [str]
    ["ziggy", "mars"]

function main()
    pair = [DIGITS[2], WORDS[1].len()]
    print(pair[0] + pair[1])
